==Trivia==
[[File:Meiyerditch Laboratories From Barrows.png|thumb|right|The Meiyerditch Laboratories as seen from Dharok's tomb.]]
* There is currently a glitch where if [[Guthan the Infested|Guthan]] is slain and he heals simultaneously, a message will appear in the player's chatbox stating {{mes|We'll finish this later...}}. This message can also appear if players run too far away from a brother in the crypts.
* Despite the fact that they appear to be ghosts, and that player unlocks the [[Dance of the Undead|Dance of the '''Undead''']] music track at Barrows, the Barrows brothers are not considered undead and are therefore not susceptible to the [[Salve amulet]] or any of its variants, nor the [[Crumble Undead]] spell. The player can only benefit from the Salve amulet by using it on the [[Skeleton (Barrows)|skeletons]] present at Barrows.
** Because they are not ghosts, they do not count toward [[Slayer task/Ghosts|ghost Slayer tasks]]. Instead, they count toward boss tasks.
* If your inventory is full when you loot the chest and you get a Barrows item, it will be dropped on the ground but will be in 100% condition. This and Falador Party Room drop parties are the only ways to drop Barrows weapons, chest pieces and leg pieces on the ground without them degrading. Barrows helms can also be dropped by using them on a [[hat stand]].
* The Barrows may be inspired by the barrows in The Lord of the Rings, which are also protected by evil spirits. Notably, both The Lord of the Rings and ''RuneScape'' call these spirits "wights", a term which (at the time of Barrows' release) was not used anywhere else in the game.
* Parts of the [[Meiyerditch Laboratories]] can be seen from the tombs of the Barrows brothers, with Dharok's tomb offering the clearest view. This is because the Barrows tombs, like all areas not on the overworld map, are actually located on a section of the world map above the [[Wilderness]] which houses all of the underground and other non-surface areas of the game.

